Pre-base-date pre-registration revision per K4 amendment pattern.
Closes V4 from Day 75 prelaunch unknowns report.

Amendment A: L15 paragraph in 'Anchor and tamper-evidence' extended to enumerate
Days 75–77 amendments alongside the existing Day 73 (May 14) carve-out:
  - Day 75 (May 15): methodology §8.2, §8.4, §10.4; plan §3.6, §5.2
  - Days 76–77 (May 16–17): methodology §11.3, curation policy silent-FALLBACK,
    pre-reg sub-index publication scope subsection (this commit)
Carve-out argument (pre-reg revisions, not §12.3 transitions, commit ordering
as provenance proof) preserved verbatim from existing paragraph.

Amendment B: New '### Sub-index publication scope' subsection inserted between
existing Eligibility section (closing at the VCMI controlled-vocabulary
paragraph) and existing Selection subsection. Ratifies Decision K2:

  Paragraph 1: VIPI v0.1.3 publishes three sub-indices (VIPI, VIPI-Open,
  VIPI-Closed) at May 18 base date; four value_kinds per sub-index (blended,
  input, output, best); twelve published series anchored at 100.00 per
  methodology §8.2; eighteen daily vipi_daily rows (the additional six
  positions — best_input and best_output across three sub-indices — are
  computed and persisted for v0.1.4 forward-compatibility but not exposed
  in the v0.1.3 publication surface).

  Paragraph 2: VIPI-Closed inaugural universe is six sole-issuer constituents
  (five Anthropic + one OpenAI, each served by a single mapped provider);
  VIPI-Closed blended and best series will be numerically identical at v0.1.3
  because per-constituent blended price equals the sole provider's posted
  price and the §8.4 cheapest-provider rule cannot identify a cheaper
  alternative when only one provider serves the constituent; structural
  identity is disclosed in each day's audit record via
  evidentiary_sub_class_per_mapping = static_by_design per methodology §11.3.2.
  Multi-provider observability for the closed-license tier is a v0.1.4-or-later
  milestone, contingent on additional mappings to closed-license models served
  by alternative providers. Paragraph-2 closing prose acknowledges the existing
  pre-reg L33 subset-not-partition disclosure: VIPI includes the six
  closed-license sole-issuer constituents alongside its open-license and other
  §5-eligible constituents.

Empirical basis: live D1 vcmi_provider_mappings query 2026-05-17 confirms six
closed-license VCMIs (5 anthropic + 1 openai), each with mapping_count=1.
Methodology §11.3.2 (commit 1cfc899) records the same distribution and
classifies all six as static_by_design.
